# Vanilla Parity Gap Tracker

Tracks divergences between Pumpkin and vanilla Minecraft 26.2 behaviour. Populated by
discovery workers; fixes land as separate branches/PRs per `CLAUDE.md` rules.

**Severity vocabulary (priority order):** Crash > Data corruption > Blocks testing > Gameplay > Cosmetic.
**Status vocabulary:** Open, PR #N, Filed #N, Fixed, Wontfix.

All PR/issue numbers below were confirmed live against `Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin` on 2026-07-27
via `gh pr view` / `gh issue view`; all were `OPEN` at that time.

## Seeded gaps (prior campaign work)

| Subsystem | Gap | Severity | Evidence | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Game rules | `randomTickSpeed` game rule was a no-op, blocking all gameplay-behaviour testing that depends on random ticks | Blocks testing | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2587 | PR #2587 |
| Commands | `execute` subcommands (e.g. `if`, `as`, `at`) never actually ran their modifiers | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2609 | PR #2609 |
| AI / Pathfinding | Pathfinder node cache was never cleared between searches, so a closed door stayed permanently unwalkable once cached | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2603 | PR #2603 |
| AI / Targeting | Target search picked the nearest entity then filtered afterward, so a single Creative player in range blanked all nearby mob aggro | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2606 | PR #2606 |
| AI / Mobs | Creeper fuse cancelled at 3 blocks instead of vanilla's 7; iron golems attacked players on sight | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2602 | PR #2602 |
| Redstone | Weighted pressure plate used integer division; blackstone button used 30 ticks instead of 20; hopper used a 9-tick transfer instead of 8 | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2589 | PR #2589 |
| Blocks | Copper waxing/scraping discarded block state, destroying double slabs; honeycomb and fire charge were never consumed | Data corruption | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2590 | PR #2590 |
| Redstone | Target block emitted no redstone power at all | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2591 | PR #2591 |
| Blocks | Note block was missing the Pling and Trumpet instruments; hopper chain compared the wrong field for its cooldown | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2611 | PR #2611 |
| World I/O | level.dat backup and file logger aborted server startup on recoverable IO errors; sky light `Empty(15)` sections were lost across save/load | Crash | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2612 | PR #2612 |
| Items | Flint and steel lit furnaces and redstone lamps; hoe wiped the snowy block state; bamboo bone meal was dead code; axe stripping left gaps | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2610 | PR #2610 |
| Plants | Twisting vines checked the wrong support face | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2604 | PR #2604 |
| Weather | Weather cycle never ran at all | Gameplay | https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC/Pumpkin/pull/2585 | PR #2585 |
